      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Plan grouped Claw agent updates",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add `openclaw.clawUpdatePlan.v1` for read-only, agent-centric reconciliation of a grouped Claw manifest\n- add `openclaw claws update <claw-or-agent> [--from <source>] --dry-run [--json]` behind `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`\n- resolve the normal target from persisted add provenance; keep `--from` as an explicit override and recovery path\n- compare effective agent capabilities, workspace files, exact package refs, MCP declarations, and agent-pinned cron declarations\n- bind the complete preview to `planIntegrity` for the consented apply slice\n- perform no mutation: planning opens existing state read-only, does not create or migrate databases, and closes every owned handle\n\n## Planning contract\n\n- direct agent ids and unambiguous installed package names resolve to one root install record\n- older supported databases without Claws tables return structured `claw_not_found`\n- missing workspaces and owned artifacts are planned for restoration; unsafe roots, operator drift, ambiguous package identity, and incomplete ownership remain blocked\n- blocked actions produce a nonzero CLI result even when no separate diagnostic blocker exists\n- independently owned packages and MCP declarations cannot be restored or changed by a Claw\n- managed, Claw-introduced resources may be removed only when inspection proves they are unchanged and otherwise unused; referenced or independently owned resources are released\n- source MCP config is compared before placeholder resolution so credentials and local substitutions do not create false drift\n\n## Capability and consent contract\n\n- capability changes use secret-safe summaries plus SHA-256 digests; raw MCP configuration and cron payloads never enter the plan model\n- effective sandbox and heartbeat values come from OpenClaw's production resolvers, including inherited and implicit defaults\n- widening workspace access, sandbox sharing, tool access, plugin code, MCP surfaces, or scheduled automation requires distinct escalation consent\n- reductions and blocked removals do not request escalation consent\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nCurrent head: `ee3b8d18037555a489652da707aa737eb3da4f0e`.\n\nAn isolated v1 Claw was persisted through the production add-plan lifecycle, then the real CLI previewed v2 with a remote OAuth MCP URL containing `URL_SECRET_123`, a secret-like tool filter, and cron message `CRON_SECRET_ABC`.\n\nHuman preview:\n\n```text\nClaw update plan: @proof/safe-preview 1.0.0 -> 2.0.0\nAgent: safe-preview\nUpdate actions: 4\nCapability changes: 5; escalations requiring distinct consent: 3\n  - agent.sandbox.mode: off -> all (change)\n  - agent.sandbox.scope: agent -> session (change)\n  ! agent.sandbox.workspaceAccess: none -> ro (change)\n  ! cronJobs.private-report: unset -> schedule cron; session isolated; payload withheld (add)\n  ! mcpServers.private-search: unset -> remote server; auth configured; tool filter configured (add)\n```\n\nJSON emitted only paths, classifications, summaries, and digests. It contained none of `secret.example.test`, `URL_SECRET_123`, `PRIVATE_TOOL_SECRET_456`, or `CRON_SECRET_ABC`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- focused capability, update-planner, and CLI coverage: 49 tests passed\n- real Claw lifecycle E2E: 8 tests passed\n- broader Claw unit coverage: 95 tests passed during the restack\n- Oxfmt, focused Oxlint, max-lines ratchet, repository guardrails, import-cycle checks, and `git diff --check` passed\n- GitHub production and test type checks passed on the prior pushed tree; the final change only resolves heartbeat defaults and splits its focused tests\n- `codex review --base ec41651ee29aa40573420ef00b038c56d155a797`: no actionable regressions\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\n- Depends on: #102427 read-only diagnostics\n- This PR: authoritative read-only update planning and consent boundary\n- Next: #102982 executes only a freshly rebuilt, unblocked, consent-matched plan\n",
        "branch": "user/giodl/claws-pr11-update-plan",
